# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code configuration: the public/private boundary
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What ships to a public clone is decided by AUDIENCE, deliberately:
#   public  - what a CONTRIBUTOR uses: shared rules, contributor skills, and
#             the read-only analysis agents.
#   private - maintainer workflows (issue/PR triage, merging, releases) and
#             marketing. These stay on the maintainer's disk, in place under
#             .claude/skills/ so Claude Code still discovers them as slash
#             commands; they are simply never committed.
#
# Two mechanics govern this list:
#   1. `.claude/*` (not `.claude/`) excludes every direct child while still
#      allowing specific subpaths to be re-included. Git cannot re-include
#      anything under a directory excluded with a trailing slash.
#   2. Adding a line here does NOT untrack an already-tracked path. Git never
#      re-ignores what is already in the index; that needs `git rm --cached`.
#      Forgetting this is exactly how the boundary drifted before.
#
# Guard: `scripts/dev/check_doc_links.py` fails CI and pre-commit when a
# tracked file links to a path this list leaves untracked, so the allowlist
# and the documentation cannot silently disagree again.
.claude/*

# Public: path-scoped AI rules are shared conventions (subprocess security,
# cross-platform testing, adapter patterns) that apply to all contributors.
!.claude/rules/

# Public: read-only analysis agents, plus the guide describing their format.
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/PERSONA_GUIDELINES.md

# Public: contributor skills. Re-include the directory, re-exclude its
# contents, then allowlist per skill - anything absent here stays private.
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/INDEX.md
!.claude/skills/references/
!.claude/skills/jmo-adapter-generator/
!.claude/skills/jmo-ci-debugger/
!.claude/skills/jmo-compliance-mapper/
!.claude/skills/jmo-dashboard-builder/
!.claude/skills/jmo-documentation-updater/
!.claude/skills/jmo-e2e-verify/
!.claude/skills/jmo-profile-optimizer/
!.claude/skills/jmo-refactoring-assistant/
!.claude/skills/jmo-security-hardening/
!.claude/skills/jmo-systematic-debugging/
!.claude/skills/jmo-target-type-expander/
!.claude/skills/jmo-test-fabricator/

